     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all, <div><br></div><div>I&#39;m currently working with the &quot;08_spatio_temporal.R&quot; practical, kindly provided by the inlabru team (thank you!) at <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/inlabru.org/inlabru/tutorials/practicals?authuser=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sites.google.com/inlabru.org/inlabru/tutorials/practicals?authuser%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441811057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2PuxxhNdQGkyuo-JB0HMfS\">https://sites.google.com/inlabru.org/inlabru/tutorials/practicals?authuser=0</a>. For this practical, I was wondering how one can extract yearly density based on the built up ST model? </div><div><br></div><div>Looking forward any support,</div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Kevin</div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FktQ1UDSIcF-IFLmsxJYd9DETcgybxMx/view?usp=drive_web\" style=\"color:inherit;font-size:22px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;text-align:center\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FktQ1UDSIcF-IFLmsxJYd9DETcgybxMx/view?usp%3Ddrive_web&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441811057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0GxIZ2M-Ii7y2dWb9594af\"><div style=\"width:190px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block\"><div><img src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/EbZzthG-9sS_s2lU2nDNJgFq-gRkXy7nXJGR_UcTFN8OcTTSrj5mZ_AOUCdU2fkDcqKbdPoJr7C8SkVjnHA98p1TMthZTNrKWp3Vg3PmeloEJhsm5-yELxd0Lqioj-CWkina=s0-d-e1-ft#https://drive-thirdparty.googleusercontent.com/128/type/application/octet-stream\" alt=\"As is\" style=\"border-width:initial;border-style:none\"></div></div></div><div style=\"overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block;color:rgb(17,85,204);font-size:14px;margin-right:25px;margin-left:25px;width:142.5px\">08_spatio_temporal.R</div></a></div>"
